  "body": "Split from #3186. PR for #3186 does the asset selection, the catalog check and `plan::may_run_ignored` for directory suites. This issue holds the `quick.rs` part.\n\nToday `quick.rs` runs the whole binary of a directory suite in these cases:\n\n- `map_modules` (`xtask/src/quick.rs` about line 181) joins the Gate maps of all the module files of a suite. A src change selects the whole binary.\n- A change outside the `#[test]` fns of one submodule sets `p.whole` (`quick.rs` about lines 103-133).\n\nChange `quick.rs`:\n\n1. Match each Gate map for each source file (`suites::Source`), not for the joined text.\n2. When only some submodules match, or when one submodule changes outside its test fns, pass a libtest module filter: `--test <suite> <submod>::`.\n3. Run the whole binary only when `main.rs` or a shared module changes.\n\nThis needs a new pick kind (a module filter for each binary) in `Picks`, in `describe` and in `steps`.\n\nDone means: `xtask` unit tests show that a change in one submodule of a directory suite plans `--test <suite> <submod>::`, and that a change in `main.rs` plans the whole binary.\n\nA second item from the #3186 work: `may_run_ignored` keeps the old rule for a flat suite. A `mod x;` line makes a flat suite heavy. About 175 flat suites with `mod common;` and no `#[ignore]` in their files get a heavy step at the cut (measured with `cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`). A walk of `suites::sources` for flat suites too removes these steps. Do this only with a review of the cut plan.\n\nPart of #919.\n",
